    docs: document REQUIRE_TIER gate + INTERRUPTOR_LOG_LEVEL, fix test-count rot and PATH claim (DOC-10, DOC-11, DOC-12, DOC-13)
    
    - DOC-10: README env table gains TERMINAL_JAIL_REQUIRE_TIER — installer-only
      fail-closed containment gate (values pidns|fs|full; unset default = advisory
      probe report that never blocks; unmet demand = exit 1 before the final
      'done.' line quoting the probe's own diagnosis; invalid value = exit 1 at
      parse time). Anchored to install.sh:298/:492 and install.sh:1360-1420.
      docs/quickstart.md 3a adds the same gate after the install command block.
    - DOC-11: README firewall section documents TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_LOG_LEVEL
      (default WARNING, read at plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/config.py:53;
      standard Python log levels, matched upper-cased, empty falls back to WARNING
      per config.py:39; applies to the interruptor engine's logging configuration —
      today config-only, no other module reads it).
    - DOC-12: README at-a-glance drops the stale hardcoded '~1,400 tests' for the
      derived-not-restated pattern used by the Rule catalog (README.md:460): the
      collect-only command plus the number at refresh time (1660, matching live
      collection). Version label kept accurate: v1.2.0 shipped, v1.3.0 held per
      release row RELEASE-TJ-008.
    - DOC-13: README install paragraph now states both PATH behaviors: the
      installer APPENDS the marked '# terminal-jail' PATH block (an export line
      naming the actual install directory) to the first of ~/.profile,
      ~/.bash_profile, ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc that exists, and also prints the exact
      export to use immediately; --uninstall removes the marked block (linked to
      the Uninstall section). Matches the TJ-GAP-065 logic in install.sh and
      resolves the disagreement with the Uninstall section (README ~line 187).
    
